WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.036
 Justin, Nic, congratulations.

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:06.239
You fellas are in the final
round of this competition.

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:07.941
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:13.779
to recreate this iconic
weapon from history, a pair

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:16.916
of Frankish throwing axes.

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:17.917
Good luck.

00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:18.851
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:19.719
 Good luck, man.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:20.420
 Yeah, to you, man.

00:00:23.922 --> 00:00:25.424
It feels great to be back home.

00:00:25.491 --> 00:00:30.062
I have to make a pair of
Frankish throwing axes.

00:00:30.162 --> 00:00:31.431
There's a lot of
subtle curves to them,

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:33.599
so it's going to be
a real challenge.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.434
I'm going to take my
piece of mild steel.

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:38.604
I'm going to forge it out, and
then I'm going to fold it over

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.406
on itself, and then
I'm going to fit it

00:00:40.472 --> 00:00:42.442
for a bit of high-carbon
steel in the middle.

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:44.243
I think that might work.

00:00:44.343 --> 00:00:46.879
Mild steel doesn't like
to weld at the heats

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:48.648
that carbon steel does.

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:49.549
Hopefully she welds.

00:00:53.052 --> 00:00:54.754 line:7%
NIC: So I'm really excited.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.088
We've made it to round three.

00:00:56.155 --> 00:00:57.756
I'm ready to get sweating
and get some sparks

00:00:57.823 --> 00:00:59.325
thrown on this thing.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:02.828
So the plan today is I'm going
to take some 1018 mild steel.

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:06.432 line:0%
We're going to start by drilling
two holes, go in with a drift,

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:09.736 line:0%
chisel it out, and start forming
our eye on both of these.

00:01:13.372 --> 00:01:15.241
It looks like a good
eye right there.

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:17.376
It's time to really
profile this thing,

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:18.611
so I'm taking it to
the power hammer.

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:20.913
That way they move
a whole lot easier.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.781
So I have the
profile forged out.

00:01:22.848 --> 00:01:24.116
I have the eyes drifted.

00:01:24.183 --> 00:01:26.018
I'm feeling pretty
good about day one,

00:01:26.118 --> 00:01:29.122
but we've got a whole
lot more work to do.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:32.859
 It's the morning of day
two, and I'm pretty tired.

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:36.495
Yesterday I was able to get both
my axes forge welded together.

00:01:36.562 --> 00:01:39.131
Now I just got to finish
drawing them out today.

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:41.200
I want to get that
done to shape,

00:01:41.266 --> 00:01:42.634
and it looks like it's staying--

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.136
oh, never mind.

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:45.738
It is not staying together.

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:49.508
I got a massive seam where that
forge weld was supposed to be.

00:01:49.575 --> 00:01:53.179
The weld didn't take at
the very back of this.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:55.915
So I'm going to try to
forge out this other head,

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:58.684
and almost right
away it split apart.

00:01:58.751 --> 00:01:59.552
It's no good.

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:01.420
So don't like that.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:02.889
Too [inaudible] to
even really forge

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:05.358
weld it again, so I
have to start over.

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:06.993
I don't know what these
tests are going to be,

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:08.695
but they're always brutal.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:10.830
So I need to make them strong.

00:02:10.896 --> 00:02:12.532
Hopefully they survive the test.

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:16.068
What I'm going to do is take
a piece of this mild steel,

00:02:16.168 --> 00:02:18.104
and I'm going to
forge it out to shape

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:21.007
and then grind in a slot
for the high-carbon bit.

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:22.909
I really have to get
a good weld here.

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.611
I can't afford to
start all over again.

00:02:27.913 --> 00:02:29.148 line:7%
NIC: So it's day two.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.450
The plan for the day is
to really fix those eyes

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:34.620
and really get them
to the shape I want.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:37.356
Ended up stretching
way too much material.

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:39.492
One of the eyes
ended up cracking.

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:42.762
There's no saving these,
and I'm starting to panic.

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:45.331
I mean, I don't have a whole
lot of room right there.

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.466
At this point, I'm
burning daylight.

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:51.203
I'm just going to have to
scrap it and start over.

00:02:51.303 --> 00:02:52.938
I'm going to do the wrap method.

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:55.842
Basically take a
flat bar of steel

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:58.244
and wrap it around
and eye and have

00:02:58.311 --> 00:03:01.580
a carbon-steel core running
all the way through instead

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.082
of just a bit.

00:03:03.182 --> 00:03:04.584
Don't really feel
good about it, but I'm

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:06.419
going to really power
through and work

00:03:06.485 --> 00:03:08.321
as fast and hard as possible.

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:13.159
My forge welding went good.

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:14.794
I believe they're good
enough for heat treat.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.232 line:0%
And I feel like the
heat-treat process

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:22.134 line:0%
went really well, so next
few days I can focus on

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:25.204 line:7%
fit and finish.

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:26.505 line:0%
JUSTIN: It's the
morning of day three.

00:03:26.572 --> 00:03:28.207 line:0%
I still got a little
more forging to do.

00:03:28.307 --> 00:03:29.742
The steel's nice and hot.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:32.445
Give it a couple whacks, and
it's feeling good already.

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:37.116
I'm, like, 99% sure I
have a good forge weld.

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:40.652
Go straight into the oil.

00:03:40.719 --> 00:03:43.422
Oh yeah.

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:47.426
Our axes have to have a handle,
so I cut out the hickory.

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:49.628
Now it's time to shape them.

00:03:49.695 --> 00:03:52.599
I can feel the sawdust
adhering to my cheeks.

00:03:57.636 --> 00:03:58.871 line:0%
NIC: So it's the
morning of day four.

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:00.672 line:0%
Today I'm going
to play dress up.

00:04:00.739 --> 00:04:02.574
These axes right now,
they're assembled.

00:04:02.674 --> 00:04:05.378
Then I'm going to do
some finer detail work.

00:04:08.814 --> 00:04:10.316
So they're both at the
finish that I want.

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:12.085
Now I need to go
above and beyond.

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:13.653
That's what my mom would
have wanted me to do.

00:04:13.719 --> 00:04:15.421
This was a challenge,
and I'm really

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:18.324
proud that I pulled it off.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:19.892
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:04:19.958 --> 00:04:22.829
Well, frankly, your Frankish
throwing axis look fantastic,

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:24.263
but are they lethal?

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.565
Well, to find that out,
I will take your weapons

00:04:26.665 --> 00:04:30.269
and deliver some,
well, hellish of a blow

00:04:30.369 --> 00:04:33.338
on this ballistics dummy.

00:04:33.405 --> 00:04:34.207
Justin, you're up first.

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:35.074
You ready?

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:35.808
 Sweaty to the teeth.

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:44.417
[music playing]

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:08.908
 All right, Justin, every
chop can slash this deep.

00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:11.076
Overall, sir, it'll kill.

00:05:11.143 --> 00:05:12.411
 Thank you.

00:05:12.511 --> 00:05:13.680
 All right, Nic,
it's your turn.

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:14.580
Ready to have fun?

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:15.415
 Let's do this.

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:22.722
[music playing]

00:05:42.741 --> 00:05:45.644
 All right, Nic,
upon impact, crushes

00:05:45.744 --> 00:05:47.779
the face easily and the head.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:52.150
Your edges, they dig in
with every chop and slash.

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:53.152
It will kill.

00:05:53.219 --> 00:05:53.885
 Thanks, Doug.

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:54.620
DOUG: Good job.

00:05:57.423 --> 00:06:00.793
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the strength test.

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:03.996
I will be throwing
your Frankish throwing

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:06.465
axes into this large wall.

00:06:06.532 --> 00:06:07.299
Justin, you're up first.

00:06:07.366 --> 00:06:08.066
You ready for this?

00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:08.767
 Yeah.

00:06:08.834 --> 00:06:09.569
Let's do it.

00:06:17.376 --> 00:06:21.848
[music playing]

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:42.467
 Well, Justin, there is
a ding on this blade right

00:06:42.534 --> 00:06:44.971
here where my finger is.

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:47.140
Your handles are comfortable.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:49.008
The problem I have
with them, this bulb

00:06:49.108 --> 00:06:51.677
is more fitted for a
fighting ax as retention.

00:06:51.744 --> 00:06:54.046
A throwing ax, you kind
of want to let it go.

00:06:54.146 --> 00:06:56.181
But, in all, your axes held up.

00:06:56.248 --> 00:06:56.915
Nice job.

00:06:57.015 --> 00:06:58.083
 Thank you.

00:06:58.184 --> 00:06:59.084
 Nic, you're up.

00:06:59.151 --> 00:06:59.818
You ready for this?

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:00.620
 Let's do this.

00:07:05.057 --> 00:07:09.562
[music playing]

00:07:22.741 --> 00:07:25.678
 Well, Nic, your
edges held up great.

00:07:25.744 --> 00:07:27.479
I can't even tell that
they've been thrown.

00:07:27.546 --> 00:07:29.715
Your handles show no damage.

00:07:29.815 --> 00:07:30.450
Nice job.

00:07:33.886 --> 00:07:36.555
 All right, bladesmiths,
this is our sharpness test,

00:07:36.622 --> 00:07:38.824
the foot-soldier attack.

00:07:38.891 --> 00:07:41.994
This is all about what
the edges of your weapon

00:07:42.094 --> 00:07:45.998
will do on the protective
clothing of this foot soldier.

00:07:46.065 --> 00:07:46.832
Justin, you're up first.

00:07:46.899 --> 00:07:47.600
You ready?

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:48.166
 Yeah.

00:07:48.233 --> 00:07:48.868
Kill it.

00:07:52.972 --> 00:07:57.210
[music playing]

00:08:13.925 --> 00:08:16.395
 All right, Justin,
your edges over here,

00:08:16.462 --> 00:08:18.497
as you can see on
the clothing on this,

00:08:18.563 --> 00:08:21.300
it cuts right into
this foot soldier.

00:08:21.367 --> 00:08:24.803
Overall, sir, your
weapons, it will cut.

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:25.604
 Cool.

00:08:25.704 --> 00:08:26.572
 All right, Nic,
your turn, sir.

00:08:26.639 --> 00:08:27.573
Are you ready?

00:08:27.673 --> 00:08:28.741
 Play some good music.

00:08:37.149 --> 00:08:41.587
[music playing]

00:08:52.698 --> 00:08:56.702
 All right, Nic, no glinting
or rolls on your edges.

00:08:56.769 --> 00:08:59.037
Sharp with every cut
that went through.

00:08:59.104 --> 00:09:00.071
It will cut.

00:09:00.138 --> 00:09:02.174
 Thank you.

00:09:02.274 --> 00:09:05.210
 All right, bladesmiths,
you guys have brought in some

00:09:05.277 --> 00:09:09.048
high-quality, competitive,
and nicely matched Frankish

00:09:09.148 --> 00:09:11.784
throwing axes, but only one of
you can be the "Forged in Fire"

00:09:11.851 --> 00:09:12.552
champion.

00:09:16.188 --> 00:09:17.589
Nic, congratulations.

00:09:17.656 --> 00:09:19.724
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:19.825 --> 00:09:23.261
Justin, unfortunately your
Frankish throwing axes

00:09:23.328 --> 00:09:24.863
did not make the cut.

00:09:24.963 --> 00:09:26.832
 Justin, both sets
of axes performed well

00:09:26.899 --> 00:09:28.467
in all of our tests,
so this basically

00:09:28.567 --> 00:09:30.035
came down to that
small amount of damage

00:09:30.135 --> 00:09:33.372
you took in the strength
test and the overall design

00:09:33.439 --> 00:09:34.874
of your axes.

00:09:34.974 --> 00:09:35.974
 Yes, sir.

00:09:36.041 --> 00:09:37.943
 Justin, you did a great
job, but at this time

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:42.448
I have to ask you to please
surrender your blades.

00:09:42.514 --> 00:09:43.481
 I just came here.

00:09:43.548 --> 00:09:44.683
I did good.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:46.252
I think I represented
myself well.

00:09:46.318 --> 00:09:48.353
And I think, if nothing
else, these tests show that I

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:49.322
can make a working blade.

00:09:52.091 --> 00:09:53.326
 Nic, congratulations.

00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:54.827
You're the "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:09:54.927 --> 00:09:58.030
and that's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:58.097 --> 00:09:59.031
Good job, man.

00:09:59.131 --> 00:10:02.467
Please present your
axes to the judges.

00:10:02.534 --> 00:10:04.737
 This experience
was incredible.

00:10:04.803 --> 00:10:07.339
I had so much fun.

00:10:07.439 --> 00:10:09.241
I came here to win for my mom.

00:10:09.341 --> 00:10:15.113
She was my biggest fan, and I've
done exactly what I plan to do.

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:17.282
Oh my gosh.

00:10:17.383 --> 00:10:19.218
I did it, Mom.

